{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVjXRkYAyqoB7R6UPnoJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about error handling in a batch processing loop. Specifically, they want to know what happens if an auth token expires while processing a page of items.\n\nLooking at the code:\n```python\nfor page in pages:\n    for item in page.items:\n        client.push(item, token=token)   # raises AuthExpired\n    checkpoint(page.id)\n```\n\nThe issue is that if `AuthExpired` is raised during the inner loop (while processing items in a page), the exception will propagate up and out of both loops, causing the program to crash or stop. The checkpoint is only called AFTER all items in a page are processed successfully.\n\nSo if an `AuthExpired` exception occurs on item 5 of a 10-item page:\n- Items 1-4 will have been pushed\n- Items 5-9 will never be attempted\n- The checkpoint for that page will NOT be called\n- The next iteration would restart the page from the beginning (assuming the pages list is re-run)\n\nThis means:\n1. **Resume point**: It will restart from the failed page, not the failed item\n2. **Lost progress**: Items 1-4 were already pushed, so they might get pushed again if you just retry the whole page (duplication risk)\n3. **No sub-checkpoint**: There's no way to know which items within a page were successfully pushed\n\nThe user is likely asking this because they're designing error recovery logic and want to understand the current behavior.\n\nI should explain:\n1. What currently happens (restarts the page)\n2. Why that's problematic (duplication, repeated work)\n3. What they might want instead (sub-checkpoints, tracking per-item state, refreshing token before page)","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6942,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6942},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"d750b25a-c742-4403-8692-328598c0322b","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:40:52.814Z","request_id":"req_011CdVjXMSLQRTHY1A43BczV"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVjXRkYAyqoB7R6UPnoJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It **restarts from the failed page**, not the failed item—and that's a problem.\n\nWhen `AuthExpired` raises on item 5 of 10, the exception propagates out of both loops without calling `checkpoint(page.id)`. On the next run, items 1–4 get pushed again (duplication risk) before hitting the same error on item 5.\n\nYou need sub-checkpoints or item-level tracking:\n\n```python\nfor page in pages:\n    processed = load_checkpoint(page.id) or set()\n    for item in page.items:\n        if item.id in processed:\n            continue\n        try:\n            client.push(item, token=token)\n            processed.add(item.id)\n            checkpoint_item(page.id, item.id)  # Save after each item\n        except AuthExpired:\n            refresh_token()  # Or re-raise and let caller retry\n            # Next run skips already-processed items\n    checkpoint_page(page.id)\n```\n\nOr, if you want to avoid duplication entirely, refresh the token *before* it expires:\n\n```python\nfor page in pages:\n    if token_expires_soon():\n        token = refresh_token()\n    for item in page.items:\n        client.push(item, token=token)\n    checkpoint(page.id)\n```\n\nWhich approach fits depends on: do you need to resume mid-page (async/long-running), or can you just refresh proactively?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6942,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6942},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"571fe895-d0eb-4647-a5f1-9ead670b5a12","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:40:56.481Z","request_id":"req_011CdVjXMSLQRTHY1A43Bc